  "description": "GUJROT crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P 21 21 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H209 Cl1 N12 Nd9 O67 P12 13+,13(Cl1 O4 1-),18(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd6 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd7 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd8 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd9 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.889-4.204 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.79-117.31°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd9(OH)(Hpmp)12(ClO4)(H2O)26](ClO4)13·18H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 26 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
